ion Industrial policy is  a huge part of that Xi Jinping can't  create a flourishing Marxist China if  they have no control over the production  of Advanced Technologies so that's the  real reason why Taiwan is so important  the real question is why hasn't C  already invaded Taiwan he has the power  he needs to launch an invasion and the  military has been planning and preparing  for years well Taiwan is not an easy  target even though it's much smaller  than mainland China conditions in the  Taiwan Strait are treacherous the  beaches are heavily fortified and the  Taiwanese military has built up ground  defenses for years Joe Biden has also  continually made statements that America  will defend Taiwan from unprovoked  invasions so for now C is biding his  time building up his military and  waiting until there is an opportune  moment but he's also had other problems  to deal with for the last two years  kovid has presented new challenges and  unexpectedly new opportunities for Xi  Jinping when the virus first broke out  in Wuhan C tried to sweep it under the  rug his internet sensors blocked any  mention of the virus and even doctors  with first-hand experience were silenced  this policy backfired though and it  quickly became clear that the virus was  going to spread across the globe so C  pivoted from a strategy of ignoring the  threat of kovid to one of Maximum fear  he locked down entire cities restricted  travel and ramped up the surveillance  State fear of the virus was enough of an  excuse to start tracking every single  Citizen's physical location at all times  it was an entirely new level of control  but it was working C had been built his  surveillance system slowly over time but  covid provided a breakthrough now anyone  could be tracked ostensibly to reduce  covet infections but it's impossible to  ignore how this further empowers the  police state as Draconian as the zero  coveted policy was it did work at least  for a few years the lockdowns prevented  the virus from spreading but  unemployment was on the rise and the  economic toll began to climb during the  Shanghai lockdowns the local economy  shrunk 14 and more and more young people  were out of work it's important to  understand what Xi Jinping was thinking  around this time it was clear that  lockdowns hurt economic growth but this  actually wasn't that big of a problem  China had been growing rapidly for  decades and so the population was quite  happy with how things were going  generally yes obviously these lockdowns  were a setback but average citizens were  still looking at the general upward  Trend and willing to sacrifice for the  greater good there were other factors to  consider as well compared to the West  China doesn't have the same level of  Hospital infrastructure they never  approved mRNA vaccines and they never  developed a base level of natural  immunity Xi Jinping had plenty of good  reasons to enforce lockdowns but those  might have just been covered to allow  him to further consolidate power after  all in October of 2022 China held the  20th National Party Congress all eyes  were on Xi Jinping who should have  stepped down if he was following the  typical succession plan that Chinese  leaders had been adhering to for the  past few decades but that's not what  happened C had successfully dispatched  every political opponent cemented his  hold on the Communist party and  guaranteed that he could rule  indefinitely it wasn't entirely  unexpected but many Chinese citizens  took issue with this aggressive decision  exact statistics about XI jinping's  popularity are hard to come by for  obvious reasons in the wake of C's third  term announcement even the letter N was  banned on social media this is because  people were simply posting n equals 3 or  n equals infinity to comment on the  number of terms he might serve even  though I've tried to cover as much as  possible about Xi Jinping there are  still tons of gaps in this story his  whole life is shrouded in secrecy and  unbiased reporting is very hard to come  by that's why it's so important to  support the sources who made all this  possible I'll leave links to additional  information down below the story is  still evolving too China and the United  States have been on a collision course  for years and a battle for the control  of the semiconductor industry is heating  up if you want to understand how Xi  Jinping is thinking about China's  artificial intelligence strategy just  watch this video next thanks for  watching
 

